e final. She must give a vote now. She can vote B, with reasoning that A lacks evidence on key criteria, and B's strengths outweigh concerns.\n\nShe should reference James's answer that no info on A's reliability/stress, and her own notes: A anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized, regarded as show-off, not open to new ideas. So A has strengths but also concerns, and missing reliability/stress data. So B remains best.\n\nThus public message: I agree with James and Emily that B is best, because A lacks evidence on reliability and stress, and has other concerns. Vote B.\n\nProceed."}
